{"name":"Outback","hex":"#c9a375","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"outback","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The most remote and desolate areas of Australia; the desert and areas too arid for growing crops."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characteristic of the most remote and desolate areas of Australia; very remote from urban areas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outback"}],"entries":[{"title":"Outback","blocks":[{"text":"The Outback is a remote, vast, sparsely populated area of Australia. It is more remote than what Australians call \"the bush\". While often envisaged as being arid, the Outback regions extend from the northern to southern Australian coastlines and encompass a number of climatic zones, including tropical and monsoonal climates in northern areas, arid areas in the \"red centre\" and semi-arid and temperate climates in southerly regions. The total population is estimated at 607,000 people."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Mount_Conner%2C_August_2003.jpg/330px-Mount_Conner%2C_August_2003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outback","wikidata":"Q569073"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Yalgoo_Shire.jpg/500px-Yalgoo_Shire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Yalgoo_Shire.jpg/1280px-Yalgoo_Shire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Yalgoo_Shire.jpg/500px-Yalgoo_Shire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tourism sign post in Yalgoo, Western Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYalgoo_Shire.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/West_MacDonnell_National_Park.JPG/500px-West_MacDonnell_National_Park.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/West_MacDonnell_National_Park.JPG/500px-West_MacDonnell_National_Park.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"MacDonnell Ranges in the Northern Territory are found in the centre of the mainland.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWest_MacDonnell_National_Park.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Fitzgerald_River_National_Park_DSC04436.JPG/500px-Fitzgerald_River_National_Park_DSC04436.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Fitzgerald_River_National_Park_DSC04436.JPG/500px-Fitzgerald_River_National_Park_DSC04436.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fitzgerald River National Park in Western Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFitzgerald_River_National_Park_DSC04436.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/ISS007_Gosses_Bluff.jpg/500px-ISS007_Gosses_Bluff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/ISS007_Gosses_Bluff.jpg/1280px-ISS007_Gosses_Bluff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/ISS007_Gosses_Bluff.jpg/500px-ISS007_Gosses_Bluff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gosses Bluff crater, one of a number of meteor impact craters that can be found across outback Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AISS007_Gosses_Bluff.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/RFDS_emergency_landing_strip_sign.jpg/500px-R